## Summary

I found and fixed the off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The bug was using `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]` to access the first word. This caused:
- The function to return the second word instead of the first ('world' instead of 'hello')
- An IndexError when there was only one word (no index 1 exists)

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` since list indexing starts at 0. All tests now pass successfully.
